@@ -1,216 +0,0 @@
-//! `leafdump` -- the regression training-data dump for the leaf evaluation
-//! (`docs/LEAFREG.txt` at the repo root; `bots::weighted::eval::WeightKey`'s
-//! 162-coordinate linear scoring function). Where `bin/agreefit.rs` fits
-//! weights against which MOVE a strong human chose (a ranking problem over
-//! candidates), this binary produces the corpus for a different fit
-//! entirely: given the STATE a real human decision was faced from, what did
-//! the game eventually come to for that seat? One row per decision point,
-//! not per candidate move.
-//!
-//! # Reused, not restated
-//!
-//! * [`tta::replay_common::replay_game`] (`record_decisions: true`) -- the
-//!   SAME decision-point walker `bin/agreefit.rs`/`bin/humandata.rs` already
-//!   use. This file adds no second replay walker.
-//! * [`tta::bots::weighted::eval::linear_features`] -- the SAME feature
-//!   vector `evaluate` itself is proven (by
-//!   `bots::weighted::eval::tests::
-//!   linear_features_dotted_with_the_champion_reproduces_evaluate_on_real_replayed_bgo_positions`)
-//!   to dot-product-reproduce, on hundreds of real positions from this exact
-//!   corpus -- not a second, drifting reimplementation of the evaluator's
-//!   arithmetic.
-//! * [`tta::game::scores`] -- the engine's own per-seat final culture total,
-//!   the same array `game::winners` reads to decide who won.
-//!
-//! # Column order
-//!
-//! `game_id, players, seat, round, <one column per WeightKey::ALL, in ITS
-//! declaration order>, win, final_score, final_rank`. The feature columns
-//! are never a hand-written list -- see [`write_header`], which walks
-//! `WeightKey::ALL` directly, so a 163rd key added to the enum widens this
-//! file's output with no edit here at all.
-//!
-//! # Outcome labels
-//!
-//! `win`/`final_score`/`final_rank` all come from [`tta::game::scores`]
-//! (culture by player index, snapshotted after `finish_game` folds in every
-//! end-of-game bonus -- see that function's own doc comment), which is only
-//! available when [`tta::replay_common::GameResult::engine_scores`] is
-//! `Some`, i.e. the replay reached a real `state.game_over` with no
-//! [`tta::replay_common::Mismatch`] along the way. A game that stops short
-//! contributes ZERO rows -- there is no partial-game, no-outcome row in this
-//! file, because a decision with no verified eventual result is not
-//! training data, it's noise. `win` is `final_score == max(final_score over
-//! all seats)`, ties sharing the win, exactly [`tta::game::winners`]'s
-//! fallback branch -- the ONE case this proxy does not special-case is
-//! §5.11's `forced_winner` (a resignation naming a winner independent of
-//! score), because [`tta::replay_common::GameResult`] does not expose the
-//! final `GameState` `forced_winner` lives on to check it (see
-//! `LEAFREG.txt`'s outcome-labels section for how many games this could
-//! plausibly touch).
-//!
-//! # Legality: public information only
-//!
-//! `linear_features` reads a rival's `hand_civil` (civil-card) IDENTITY --
-//! `bots::weighted::cards::rival_hand_potential`'s own doc comment and
-//! `docs/RULES_SPEC.md` §2.6 both establish this is legally public (cards
-//! taken from the row are witnessed by every player at the table, the "open
-//! civil cards convention") -- but never a rival's `hand_military` identity
-//! or any deck's shuffle ORDER (only the public `.len()`/count of either).
-//! [`tta::bots::weighted::eval::tests::
-//! linear_features_never_depends_on_a_rivals_hidden_military_hand_card_identity`]
-//! pins this structurally (and was confirmed to catch a real regression --
-//! see that test's own doc comment and `LEAFREG.txt`'s legality section for
-//! the RED/GREEN transcript), so this binary adds no separate privacy filter
-//! of its own: it calls `linear_features` exactly as `WeightedBot` does at
-//! play time.
-//!
-//! # Regeneration
-//!
-//! ```text
-//! tar -xzf sources/bgo/journals.tar.gz -C /tmp/bgo-journals   # once
-//! cargo run --profile difftest --bin leafdump -- \
-//!     sources/bgo/index.tsv /tmp/bgo-journals/journals \
-//!     > leaf_dataset.tsv 2> leaf_dataset_report.txt
-//! ```
-
