From 98508b3467dc6fd68fc76221647245c49cc8e747 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Tarjan <github@paulisageek.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 18:19:46 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Recover the 68 TruncatedAfterGameOver human games
 (222->290)

68/789 skipped BGO journals (GAMEDROP.txt) log their duplicated trailing
"End turn" pair BEFORE the real "End of game" marker instead of after, so
finish_game's round-wrap check already flips state.game_over one line
before replay_game ever reads the marker, and `completed` never gets set.

Naively flipping `completed` there is not enough: finish_game already ran
events::evaluate_final_events off the still-fictional event piles by that
point, baking a wrong culture delta into player state before the real
"End of game" text is even reached. The fix peeks ahead for the
still-unread marker, subtracts back out the wrong award (recomputed off
the untouched fictional piles), grounds the piles for real, and re-runs
evaluate_final_events against them -- the same grounding/scoring path
every already-working game's own "End of game" branch takes, just run
after the fact for the minority whose journal orders it differently.

Gated on `!completed`, so the new branch is unreachable for every
already-working game (`completed` is already true by the time this guard
could fire) -- confirmed byte-identical leafdump output on the original
222 games, before vs after. Full leafdump run: 222->290 games verified,
63,917->84,685 decision rows. Added a regression test on real game
7522663 pinning the exact quirk, confirmed RED by reverting the fix and
re-running before restoring it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
